@startuml
' Day 2 — Task 23: Sequence Diagram — Real-Time Trip Status Update
' Hand-drawn original: docs/handwritten/day2-sequence-diagram.jpg (mandatory first)
' Shows: mobile app -> API -> database -> pub/sub -> WebSocket gateway -> dashboard
' Includes: failure branch (WebSocket disconnected) and multi-instance acknowledgement

actor Captain as CAP
participant "Mobile App" as APP
participant "API (instance 1..n)" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Redis Pub/Sub" as PUB
participant "WebSocket Gateway" as WS
participant "Dashboard Client" as DASH

CAP -> APP : taps "Start Trip"
APP -> API : POST /trips/:id/status {Started}
activate API
API -> DB : validate transition against state machine
DB --> API : legal
API --> APP : 200 OK
API -> PUB : publish trip.status.started {tripId, ts}
deactivate API

PUB -> WS : deliver event (channel shared by all instances)
WS -> DASH : push {tripId, status: Started, ts}
DASH --> WS : ack

alt WebSocket disconnected (client offline)
  WS --> WS : buffer missed event per client
  DASH -> WS : reconnect + catch-up request
  WS -> DASH : replay missed events since last ack
end

note over API, PUB : API is horizontally scaled (2+ instances);\nthe publisher and the gateway are decoupled via the channel,\nso the event reaches the client regardless of which instance handled the request

@enduml
